  <h3>FIVB Volleyball Scoring and Rotation Rules</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Rally Point System:</strong> Standard sets are played to 25 points with a mandatory 2-point advantage. If the match goes to a deciding 5th set (or 3rd set in best-of-3 format), it is played to 15 points with a 2-point advantage.</li>
    <li><strong>Side-Out and Rotation:</strong> When the receiving team wins a rally, they gain the serve and their six court players must rotate one position clockwise (Position 2 moves to Position 1 to serve).</li>
    <li><strong>Team Match Limits:</strong> Each team is permitted a maximum of two 30-second timeouts and six player substitutions per set.</li>
  </ul>
